Start();
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search GroupFields Utilities list;
register(BlockCallT);
define
    pz=0;
    pSrc="{ pz = 7; }";
    BC0 code={ pz = 0; rc = BlocK(pSrc); cerr "BC BC0pz " pz:; cerr "BC BC0rc " rc:; };
    BC1 code={ pz = 0; src := pSrc; rc = BlocK(src); cerr "BC BC1pz " pz:; cerr "BC BC1rc " rc:; };
    BC2 code={ pz = 0; src := pSrc; block := Grokking["BlocK"]; rc = *block(src); cerr "BC BC2pz " pz:; cerr "BC BC2rc " rc:; };
    BC3 code={ pz = 0; src := pSrc; BlocK(src); cerr "BC BC3pz " pz:; };
    BC4 code={ pz = 0; block := Grokking["BlocK"]; rc = *block(pSrc); cerr "BC BC4pz " pz:; cerr "BC BC4rc " rc:; };
    ;
BC0(); BC1(); BC2(); BC3(); BC4();
cerr "BLOCKCALL SENTINEL":;
stop();

What blockCallT Is

SEQ 325 R0 (2026-10-09): defect (h), seal 85 -- a rule called with a HOLDER drives the holder's
NAME text, not the held field's text. driveStep pushes the field it is handed and unwraps the
holder one line later (GroupActions.rtn, unwrapTheHolder), so BlocK(src) with src := pSrc parses
"src". Acceptance lines (SEQ 309): BlocK(code) and result = *block(code); -- both kant.

pSrc holds "{ pz = 7; }", so pz reads 7 only if the SOURCE TEXT was driven: pz is the by-value
read of what was driven, rc of what came back. A failed drive hands back nothing and rc prints
its own tag (bear-trap 26).

Rows, trunk switch off today -> intended (switch on today in brackets):
  BC0 BlocK(pSrc), the field itself -- the control   pz 7, rc 7 -> 7, 7  [7, 7]
  BC1 rc = BlocK(src), src := pSrc                    pz 0, rc rc -> 7, 7 [0, rc]
  BC2 rc = *block(src), block := Grokking["BlocK"]    pz 0, rc rc -> 7, 7 [0, rc]
      (O1's shape; switch off it ALSO loses the call at the star -- see BC4)
  BC3 BlocK(src); as a statement                      pz 0 -> 7           [0]
  BC4 rc = *block(pSrc), no holder -- separates BC2's two defects
                                                      pz 0, rc rc -> 7, 7 [7, 7]
      Switch off the star-call is lost before any drive (docs/expressionRecon.md step 1
      section 3); switch on (*block)(pSrc) calls. Not (h): (h) is the holder.

  expr-h (SEQ 325 R2): driveStep unwraps the holder at entry. Switch off BC1 and BC3 read 7, 7 and 7;
  switch on BC1, BC2 and BC3 read 7. BC2 switch off stays 0 / rc -- the star-call (BC4).

Own fixture, not rows in exprPinT: a drive of the wrong text can fail anywhere in the parse.
